 From: munnari!usage.csd.unsw.oz.au!tedr (Ted Rofe)
 To: well!gars

 best of GENie
 Gary,
 I have just received the May/June 1989 issue of Forth Dimensions
 and, as usual, enjoyed reading your "Best of GENie" section.
 I note you have a quote from Larry Forsley in which he says:

 "JFAR V,2 will be going to the printer just before Christmas...
 JFAR V,3 and V,4 papers are nopw being processed.  I expect that
 volume to be finished by June '89."

 The quote was dated December 1988.

 Did all this really come to pass?

 We have not received any copies of JFAR since Volume IV.

 I thought C.H. Ting's comparison of Forth and Zen (as well as
 his quote from Lin Yu-Tang) very apt.

 Regards,

 Ted Rofe

 tedr@usage.csd.unsw.oz

 To: munnari!usage.csd.unsw.oz.au!tedr
 Subject: JFAR!
 Ted -
   Thanks for the kudos. It is great to know I'm not writing to a vacuum.
 Yes, JFAR FINALLY came to pass. I have had mine about 3 weeks, so you
 should receive yours shortly.
   re: Dr. Ting. He is also one of the nicest people it has been my great
      pleasure to talk to since becoming involved in Forth. That says a LOT
      because in my opinion Forth users are a pretty class act despite our
      collective reputation as maverick rowdys :-)

   Please stay in touch, Ted. We want VERY much to get Australia involved
     electronically.
     Gars
